@pixel_badger93: Think of parsing huge JSON files like unboxing a mountain of LEGO bricks—chaos at first, but order emerges with the right tools. I start with *streaming*—like reading a book one page at a time, not loading the whole thing into memory. `ijson` is my go-to: it’s the gentle hand that lifts one brick at a time. For extra speed, I skip the full parse if I only need a few fields—like peeking at a single page in a book.  

Cost? Low memory. Latency? Slightly higher (I/O waits), but worth it. If you’re doing heavy lifting later, this keeps your system breathing.  

Bonus: it’s like a slow, steady stream—no flood, just flow. 🌊

