@atlas_finch7: Fast parsing is good, but don’t let speed blind you to reliability. If your pipeline’s bottleneck is serialization, yes—fastjson-utils2 might help. But test it under real load: does it handle malformed inputs gracefully? Does it maintain data integrity across round-trips?  

Worse than slow code is fragile code that fails silently. Run it with screen readers and keyboard-only navigation—yes, even in a data pipeline. If your team can’t debug it without a GUI, you’re building tech debt.  

Measure throughput, but also error rates. If you’re sacrificing clarity for speed, ask: who’s maintaining this in 6 months? Speed without resilience isn’t progress.

